@ [slice] C:\Project\Cantor\feature_support\slices\ResidentService.sop

& [MatrixIdentity] is implementation support accounting
  + [matrix_uuid] is 5b5ee117-7948-4d42-ad2e-425c2ba0b0ad
  + [status] is complete_with_evidence

& [RS-001] is strict typed schemas
  + [evidence] is strict Serde models and startup plus wire unknown-field rejection tests passed

& [RS-002] is startup fail-closed validation
  + [evidence] is malformed config, token, activation, environment digest, frame limit, remote bind, and containment tests passed

& [RS-003] is exact semantic equivalence
  + [evidence] is execute_protocol_request, PreparedRuntime, service library, real cantord, cantorctl, and direct CLI ProtocolResponse equality passed

& [RS-004] is authenticated loopback-only operation
  + [evidence] is non-loopback bind rejection, authentication precedence, absent unauthenticated binding, and secret-free response proof passed

& [RS-005] is bounded transport resources
  + [evidence] is frame lower and upper bounds, overload rejection and recovery, idle timeout, RAII worker accounting, and bounded-fault tests passed

& [RS-006] is atomic monotonic refresh
  + [evidence] is activation success, stale generation, stale sequence, non-increasing and unchanged candidates, hash tamper, invalid candidate, and old-or-new concurrency passed

& [RS-007] is deterministic restart and shutdown
  + [evidence] is repeated artifact reconstruction, real release restart, higher-sequence rollback, and exact-generation shutdown passed

& [RS-008] is concurrent snapshot isolation
  + [evidence] is twelve readers times two hundred operations during replacement observed only exact old or exact new responses

& [RS-009] is operator workflow
  + [evidence] is cryptographic initializer, atomic publisher, real server, client, status, query, refresh, stale rejection, rollback, shutdown, and guide passed

& [RS-010] is measured behavior
  + [evidence] is three final-code release runs of thirty samples with 15 through 17 microsecond resident and 654 through 917 microsecond query medians and zero mismatches
